WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.680
Salem, the 1840s.

2
00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:07.360
A dusty upper room in the
Custom-House, full of old papers.

3
00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:09.760
A man unties one package.

4
00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:15.230
Inside: a roll of yellowed paper,
and a faded scrap of red cloth.

5
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.680
"It was the capital letter A."

6
00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.520
He holds it to his chest.

7
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:22.060
He flinches, and lets it fall.

8
00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:26.380
Then the story jumps two
centuries back, to Puritan Boston.

9
00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:30.030
So why begin in an 1840s office at all?

10
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:33.100
In this mission, you'll learn
what a frame narrative is,

11
00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.230
and ask what this one is doing.

12
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.940
You'll read the moment the
Surveyor finds the letter,

13
00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:39.420
line by line.

14
00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:44.120
And you'll meet the scaffold, the platform
that holds the whole novel together.

15
00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Your mission: explain why the
story begins in that office.
